{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament\/neidhardtIII"},"metadata":{"extendedModule":"IvorTuning","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"property","modules":[{"name":"IvorTuning"}],"fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"neidhardtIII","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"WellTemperament","preciseIdentifier":"s:10IvorTuning15WellTemperamentV"}],"externalID":"s:10IvorTuning0B6SystemPA2A15WellTemperamentVRszrlE12neidhardtIIIAEvpZ::SYNTHESIZED::s:10IvorTuning15WellTemperamentV","title":"neidhardtIII","roleHeading":"Type Property","conformance":{"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"WellTemperament"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"text":"Available when","type":"text"}],"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}]}},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Neidhardt III (“Large City”; Johann Georg Neidhardt, 1724)."}],"sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivortuning\/welltemperament\/neidhardtiii"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"neidhardtIII","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"WellTemperament","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:10IvorTuning15WellTemperamentV","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament"},{"text":" { ","kind":"text"},{"text":"get","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" }","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Three fifths — C→G, G→D, D→A — are each narrowed by ⅙ of the Pythagorean comma"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(≈ 698.045 cents). Six fifths — A→E, B→F♯, F♯→C♯, C♯→A♭, E♭→B♭, B♭→F — are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each narrowed by 1\/12 of the Pythagorean comma (≈ 700.000 cents). The remaining"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"three fifths — E→B, A♭→E♭, F→C — are pure. The circle closes exactly:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"3×(1\/6) + 6×(1\/12) = 1 Pythagorean comma."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"From "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Sectio Canonis Harmonici"}]},{"type":"text","text":" (Königsberg, 1724). Differs from "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament\/neidhardtII","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"only in the placement of the sixth-comma group on the flat side: E♭→B♭ is tempered"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"here where it is pure in Neidhardt II, and F→C is pure here where it is tempered"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in Neidhardt II."}]}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning","doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament"]]},"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://IvorTuning/documentation/IvorTuning":{"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning","role":"collection","type":"topic","title":"IvorTuning","abstract":[{"text":"Musical pitch, interval, and tuning system types.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivortuning"},"doc://IvorTuning/documentation/IvorTuning/WellTemperament/neidhardtII":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Neidhardt II (“Small City”; Johann Georg Neidhardt, 1724).","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"neidhardtII"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:10IvorTuning15WellTemperamentV","text":"WellTemperament"}],"type":"topic","title":"neidhardtII","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivortuning\/welltemperament\/neidhardtii","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament\/neidhardtII","conformance":{"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Available when"}],"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"WellTemperament"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}]}},"doc://IvorTuning/documentation/IvorTuning/WellTemperament/neidhardtIII":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"neidhardtIII","url":"\/documentation\/ivortuning\/welltemperament\/neidhardtiii","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament\/neidhardtIII","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Neidhardt III (“Large City”; Johann Georg Neidhardt, 1724).","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"neidhardtIII"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:10IvorTuning15WellTemperamentV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"WellTemperament"}],"conformance":{"availabilityPrefix":[{"text":"Available when","type":"text"}],"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"WellTemperament"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}]}},"doc://IvorTuning/documentation/IvorTuning/WellTemperament":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivortuning\/welltemperament","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"WellTemperament","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"WellTemperament","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A tuning system in which all twelve keys are usable but have distinct tonal characters,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"achieved by distributing the Pythagorean comma unevenly around the circle of fifths."}],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"WellTemperament","kind":"identifier"}]}}}